---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { buildBreadcrumbSchema, buildFAQSchema } from "../../lib/seo";

const pageFaqs = [
  {
    question: "How should I use CELPIP sample answers for preparation?",
    answer: "Use CELPIP sample answers to study structure, tone, and idea development patterns. Adapt patterns to your own language instead of memorizing exact responses.",
  },
  {
    question: "Are CELPIP sample answers enough for a high score?",
    answer: "Sample answers help, but high scores usually require active practice, timed responses, and feedback on your own writing and speaking output.",
  },
  {
    question: "Where can I find CELPIP sample answers on this site?",
    answer: "You can access sample-answer resources through the CELPIP writing samples page and related task-level CELPIP writing and speaking guides.",
  },
];

const pageStructuredData = [
  buildBreadcrumbSchema(Astro.site, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Blog", path: "/blog/" },
    { name: "CELPIP Sample Answers", path: "/blog/celpip-sample-answers/" },
  ]),
  buildFAQSchema(pageFaqs),
];
---

<Layout
  title="CELPIP Sample Answers | How to Use Models Without Memorizing"
  description="CELPIP sample answers strategy guide for writing and speaking: how to learn structure and language patterns without memorization traps."
  type="article"
  keywords="CELPIP sample answers, CELPIP writing samples, CELPIP speaking sample answers, CELPIP preparation"
  structuredData={pageStructuredData}
>
  <article class="section" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding-top: var(--s-6);">
    <div style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);"><a href="/blog" style="color: var(--accent);">← Back to blog</a></div>
    <header style="margin-bottom: var(--s-4);">
      <h1 style="margin: 0;">CELPIP Sample Answers Guide</h1>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: var(--s-3); color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: var(--s-2); flex-wrap: wrap;">
        <span>📅 March 14, 2026</span><span>✍️ IELTS Corner Team</span><span>⏱️ 6 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="article-content" style="line-height: 1.8;">
      <p>CELPIP sample answers are useful when you treat them as models, not scripts. The strongest students copy structure and idea flow, then produce their own language under timed conditions.</p>
      <h2>What to study in sample answers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Opening and closing sentence patterns</li>
        <li>How reasons are supported with examples</li>
        <li>Tone control for task context</li>
        <li>Transition use and paragraph flow</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What not to do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Memorize full answers and repeat them in test conditions</li>
        <li>Copy advanced vocabulary you cannot control naturally</li>
        <li>Ignore timing while focusing only on model language</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Where to practice</h2>
      <p>Use <a href="/celpip/writing/samples">CELPIP writing samples</a>, then move to the <a href="/celpip/writing/ai-feedback">AI writing lab</a> or <a href="/tutoring">tutoring</a> for personalized feedback.</p>
      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      {pageFaqs.map((item) => (
        <details class="card" style="margin-bottom: var(--s-3);">
          <summary style="cursor: pointer; font-weight: 700;">{item.question}</summary>
          <p class="muted" style="margin-top: var(--s-2); margin-bottom: 0;">{item.answer}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>